  "continuity": "All domain 122 plus bound-room repository 3 passed on the same manifest as the initial gateway 46, whose existing 38 regressions all passed. Two new room-test fixture failures were fixed, and only the existing retained/HTTP integration test files were expanded. The corrected room 8, retained 32 and initial API 141 share identical unchanged inputs. Only the HTTP fixture then changes to use two distinct employees; final actual API 141 and full worker 138 share an identical unchanged manifest. Production source did not change after policy acceptance. Existing V135 schema is unchanged.",
  "resolvedFixtureFailures": [
    "The initial API run had two new HTTP fixture failures: the old native helper creates multiple sessions for the same administrator. The corrected tests provision distinct employees in distinct companies and assert those boundaries before opening the room. Existing runtime peer rejection was correct; production was unchanged.",
    "The first policy compile failed because an existing worker Queue test stub lacked the new room lookup method. Added an unused fail-fast stub; no production policy changed.",
    "The initial room expiry test attempted to edit token expiry without the required generation update. It now uses a valid short rotation under current native authority, lets that token expire, then expires native access. The database trigger was not weakened.",
