    "Typed exact bound-room lookup uses existing V131 participant root RLS and unique space/room identity with a two-row bound. Pure policy validates original account/user/creator/origin/binding/time metadata; malformed and duplicate rows fail closed.",
    "Room discovery only supplies sorted guard IDs. Current caller admission precedes either discovery outcome, and no provider slot is claimed after failed discovery. Unknown/unbound/foreign rooms never reach provider I/O.",
    "Current confirmed peer selection and own publication are pinned with the exact bound room. Offline short receiving credentials may expire; offboarding blocks new sends while owned room metadata remains.",
    "Signed own keys are detached and verified inside provider I/O. Optional Matrix device and sender curve fields must match the original device; SDK payloads omitting those fields remain valid. Original ciphertext/session/transaction IDs pass unchanged.",
    "PostgreSQL races cover recipient changes before send and after either provider outcome, invalid own publication, cancelled key reads, interrupted sends, native revocation after failed room discovery and exact lease cleanup. All provider calls are outside SQL transactions.",
    "Actual Synapse returns one original room event ID across repeat send and provider restart; the offline peer history has exactly one matching original ciphertext/session/sender event. This room-event behavior is measured separately from to-device replay.",
    "Completed LEGACY devices retry original ciphertext and old HRIS_ device IDs in both a retained original room and a new cross-company group room, without changing original identity/key provenance. Existing offline/current-other-membership and hard-revocation assertions remain.",
    "Actual HTTP tests reject wrong/duplicate/query credentials, malformed/plaintext/oversized requests and unrelated rooms; current receiver revocation after provider acceptance withholds the obsolete event ID. Company/native regression routes and full worker DI graph pass."
